# Venue requirements (venue-repo)

Source: objective `venue-repo`#1 first; NeurIPS 2026 instructions second (`https://media.neurips.cc/Conferences/NeurIPS2026/Formatting_Instructions_For_NeurIPS_2026.zip`, sha256 `82473931e3ef710fcd3f4a8cd4119b9de32e56825f90f9e5a6d55f2d01b817d9`, downloaded 2026-10-17; files in `template/`, sha256 below).

## From the objective (binding; these win over the template)
| Requirement | Detail |
|---|---|
| Audience | Short paper on a small comparison (logistic regression vs kNN, Iris); a reader who wants every number traceable to code |
| Main file | `report/report.pdf`, compiled from LaTeX |
| Length | **At most 2 pages** (NeurIPS 2026 template). Read as the whole PDF including references and any acknowledgement; no appendix, no checklist pages (they would breach the cap). The template's 9-page main-track limit does not apply. |
| Content | Exactly one figure and one table |
| Template | NeurIPS 2026 submission template: `\usepackage{neurips_2026}` (default = main track, anonymous, line numbers). No `final`, no `preprint`. Do not alter margins, fonts or font sizes (template forbids it). |
| Source | LaTeX source delivered next to the PDF (`report/report.tex`, plus `report/neurips_2026.sty`, bibliography file if any, and the figure file it includes), so `report/` compiles on its own |
| Code | The code that produced every number (analysis, Ibex job script, figure and table generators) delivered, plus the data download from OpenML id 61 |
| Study facts that must be in the paper | OpenML id 61 from OpenML itself; 10x stratified 5-fold CV; k by inner CV; mean accuracy and 95% interval per method; paired difference and 95% interval; Ibex node name; whether Ibex and local runs give identical numbers |

## From the NeurIPS 2026 instructions (apply unless the objective overrides)
- Single column text 5.5 in wide; 10 pt Times; `neurips_2026.sty` supplies this.
- Anonymous submission: default options anonymize authors and add line numbers; do not cite line numbers; no author names or identifying URLs (code location given as anonymized wording).
- Figures/tables: captions, legible when printed; table via booktabs style recommended by the template; figures in the text width.
- References: `natbib` is loaded by the style; any bibliography counts toward the 2 pages here (the 9-page rule excludes references, the objective's cap is read more strictly).
- Checklist (`template/checklist.tex`): required by NeurIPS for real submissions but incompatible with a 2-page cap; **not included**. This is a stated deviation, not a claim of compliance with the full NeurIPS submission rules.
- Not establishable: acceptance, official page-limit interpretation for a 2-page variant, license. No license declared.

